      "body": "## Overview\n\nRemove A100 CI steps that the pipeline generator no longer emits. The A100 fleet is retired, and ci-infra#577 drops every step whose device is a100.\n\nLegacy-test tracker: A5\n\n## Claims\n\n- Removes the `(A100) Batch Invariance` step in `misc.yaml`, the two `(A100) LM Eval Humming ... TEMPORARY` steps and the commented-out 4xA100 block in `lm_eval.yaml`, and the five `humming/config-a100-*.txt` shard lists.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `pre-commit run` on the changed files passes, including test tethering (no test loses its CI job).\n- A repo-wide grep (vllm/, tests/, benchmarks/, examples/, tools/, docs/, .buildkite/) finds no remaining reference to any deleted file.\n- Edited yamls parse; the test-tethering hook passes.\n- GPU tests not run locally; CI covers them.\n\n## Details\n\n- Left for a follow-up: `(A100) Distributed` and `(A100) NixlConnector PD + Spec Decode acceptance` still exist only to emit their live MI355 mirrors, so they first need to become standalone AMD steps.\n- Reviewer call: `humming/Qwen3-4B-mixed-quant-RTN-humming.yaml` is kept although only the deleted A100 lists referenced it, in case it should move to an H100 list.\n- Split out of the original #60591 cleanup so each part reviews on its own. Part of a legacy-test audit; no test that currently runs is affected. Not a duplicate: open-PR searches found no PR removing these files.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code an